00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.919 align:start position:0%
 
going together  pressure streak  what does it take to transform the  familiar if a new game armed you with a  standard array of weapons put you in the  kind of rundown villages and industrial  landscapes you've seen a dozen times  before and ask you to shoot your enemies  defend a location or capture a flag how  could that game be anything but overly  familiar it would have to change  something major something with the power  to affect every aspect of the game  something like movement titanfall  reinvents player movement and in doing  so reinvents what it feels like to play  a competitive shooter the freedom to  leap climb and run along walls elevates  Titan Falls fast-paced combat too  thrilling Heights and this freewheeling  action intertwines beautifully with the  brutish tactical Titan battles titanfall  is a leap forward for shooters a game  that combines the vibrant and new with  the tried and true to create something  special the key to titanfall success is  mobility the way you maneuver through  the environments as a jump pack equipped  pilot it starts with double jumping on  two shipping crates and in two  second-story windows and moves on to  running along walls and leaping around  corners these moves are completely  dependent on the angle of your approach  and the timing of your jumps so it's  easy to get the hang of the basics as  you develop a sense for how your pilot  sticks to walls you can string together  more and more complex acrobatics  this makes simply moving around the map  both a continual pleasure and a constant  challenge as you gleefully try to  exploit every billboard building and  zipline to your advantage  the 15 diverse maps are all rich with  opportunities for creative locomotion  it's always empowering to learn the maps  in a competitive shooter but this  satisfaction is heightened in titanfall  because you're expanded mobility means  there is so much more to learn it also  means your enemies can come at you from  almost any direction brandishing one of  the fairly standard weapons or maybe the  novel auto-locking smart pistol add to  this the ability to turn almost  invisible to boost speed or to see  enemies through walls and you have a lot  of strategic considerations when  engaging foes which is more deadly a  speeding wall runner rapidly closing  distance or a cloaked enemy wall hanging  above a doorway and waiting to pounce  enemy pilots make for  opponents but the AI grunts that deploy  into combat are more like cannon fodder  they don't pose much of a threat as long  as you don't try to kick your way  through a large group of them but in  addition to making battles feel more  populated grunts service targets of  opportunity to help you level up unlock  weapon attachments and reduce your Titan  build time because in titanfall  everybody gets it Titan  and every Titan is a force to be  reckoned with armed with an array of  offensive and defensive weapons Titans  present an entirely different kind of  combat one in which shield management  use of cover and properly timed salvos  of explosive ordnance decide the victor  these slower more prolonged clashes  offer a refreshing contrast to the  speedy pilot firefights but don't think  that these two exist independently of  each other pilots can bombard Titans  from afar or hop on their backs like  mischievous monkeys Titans in turn can  punch squash and blow up pilots with  ease provided they can get a bead on  them and herein lies the magic of  titanfall two very distinct types of  combat expertly balanced and intertwines  to create chaotic conflicts brimming  with opportunities for incredible  emergent moments though titanfall  actually does tell a story within the  campaign multiplayer mode the reason you  play this multiplayer only shooter is  the stories you make yourself and with  so many clever mechanics and enticing  strategies to play with you're gonna  have some great titanfall stories to  tell

